 ahead of Hoseah TJALE (05:42:40) and Derrick TIVERS (05:53:53). Helen LUCRE won the women's race in 06:53:24, followed by Lindsay WEIGHT (07:01:23).\n\nHelen LUCRE's 06:53:24 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1952 (Trevor ALLEN, 07:00:02).\n\nIn a remarkable coincidence, Bruce FORDYCE's winning time of 05:37:01 was identical to the second to the winning time posted in 1987 — both on the same direction course.\n\nFrom a field of 10,094 entries, 8,187 runners completed the course for a 81.1% finish rate. The field comprised 7,887 men and 300 women (3.7% female). The average finish time was 09:26:05.\n\nMedals awarded: 11 Gold, 642 Silver, 7,534 Bronze. 3,125 runners (38.2%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Charles BESTER in 10:59:57.\n\nCompared to the previous up run in 1983, the field was 88.1% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 20% of the finishers, with 6,547 seniors (avg 09:24:46) and 1,640 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":0.0}